{"name":"Clerestory","hex":"#f4e6e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clerestory","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The upper part of a wall containing windows to let in natural light to a building, especially in the nave, transept and choir of a church or cathedral."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clerestory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clerestory","blocks":[{"text":"A clerestory is a high section of wall that contains windows above eye level. Its purpose is to admit light, fresh air, or both."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Stralsund%2C_st_Nikolai_%282007-01-24%29_d.JPG/330px-Stralsund%2C_st_Nikolai_%282007-01-24%29_d.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clerestory"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Monreale.jpg/500px-Monreale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Monreale.jpg/500px-Monreale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The walls of the clerestory of the basilica-shaped Cathedral of Monreale, Italy, covered with mosaics","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonreale.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/History_of_architecture_0152b.jpg/500px-History_of_architecture_0152b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/History_of_architecture_0152b.jpg/1280px-History_of_architecture_0152b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/History_of_architecture_0152b.jpg/500px-History_of_architecture_0152b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fro